# Excluded from CLI (`netlify deploy`) uploads.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE A CLI DEPLOY ONCE PUBLISHED secrets.h.
#
# Production is a git-linked build, so it only ever deploys files tracked in git and
# secrets.h — being gitignored — was never in it. But `netlify deploy` from a laptop
# uploads the publish directory verbatim and does NOT honour .gitignore, so the WiFi
# PSK and MQTT credentials went live on a draft URL. Anyone with those can publish
# garage/trigger directly and open the door with no token at all.
#
# The forced 404 redirects in netlify.toml are the second layer; this one keeps the
# bytes off Netlify entirely. Do not remove either.
esp32/
docs/
node_modules/
*.md
package.json
package-lock.json
deno.lock
